    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d473">

                <pb facs="0752" n="705" sameAs="frus:frus1955-57v03mSupp/pg705"/>

                <head>473. Telegram 1568 to Geneva<anchor n="1" xml:id="d473-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1956-02-01">February 1, 1956, 6:24
                            p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <pb facs="d473-1" n="1" type="facsimile" xml:id="d473-1"/>
                <p>1568. For Johnson. Our 1567.</p>
                <p>Both British Embassy and American Red Cross have received telegrams from Hong
                    Kong confirming Liu stated he did not wish to proceed Communist China. He is
                    being cared for by Hong Kong authorities who are investigating whether Liu has
                    any relatives in colony. American Red Cross has requested British Red Cross
                    undertake any humanitarian assistance required by Liu and British Red Cross has
                    agreed. American Red Cross telegraphing Chinese Communist Red Cross that Liu
                    unwilling proceed Communist China and that British Red Cross will render
                    assistance.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#bold">Dulles</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
